# Runtime dependencies of the backend: the file to edit by hand.
# requirements.txt is generated from it (every package pinned, with hashes)
# and is what the Docker image installs. Test-only packages go in
# requirements-dev.in, never here.
#
# After editing, regenerate both lock files from the backend/ directory:
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version "$(cat .python-version)" --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
#   uv pip compile requirements-dev.in --universal --python-version "$(cat .python-version)" --generate-hashes -o requirements-dev.txt
# Existing pins are kept unless a change needs a new one. To move pins to the
# newest allowed versions, add --upgrade (all packages) or
# --upgrade-package NAME (one package) to the first command, then run the
# second command too.
